# What must never enter a Docker build context.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 🔴 THIS IS NOT ONLY ABOUT SIZE. All three application Dockerfiles do
# `COPY . .` after installing dependencies, so without this file the HOST's
# `node_modules`, `.next` and `dist` are copied over the ones the image just
# built.
#
# That is the "stale artifact" defect this repository has a scar from: three
# leftover `next start` servers faked product defects for an hour on 2026-07-30,
# and six apps' stale `.next` builds produced `UntrustedHost` errors that read
# exactly like a live configuration fault. The same bytes reaching a container
# would be harder to see, not easier — the image would be built from a mixture
# of a clean install and whatever happened to be on the machine that ran the
# build, and it would differ between a developer's laptop and CI.
#
# 🔴 pnpm's `node_modules` IS THE WORST CASE. It is a tree of SYMLINKS into a
# content-addressed store that does not exist inside the image. Copying it in
# produces dangling links that resolve at build time on the host and fail at
# runtime in the container — which is precisely why `apps/api/Dockerfile`'s
# header explains it uses `pnpm deploy` rather than copying `node_modules`. That
# reasoning only holds if the host's copy cannot sneak in behind it.
#
# ⚠️ AN EXCLUSION HERE IS NOT A SECRET CONTROL. `.env` is listed because it must
# not be baked into a layer, but a file that has already been committed is in
# git history and this changes nothing about that. Secrets come from the
# platform's environment; this only stops a local one being copied in.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── build output and dependencies: rebuilt inside the image, always ─────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── version control and CI: a container never needs its own history ─────────
# `.git` is usually the single largest thing in the context.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── local environment and credentials ───────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── editor, OS and tooling noise ────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude

# ── tests, fixtures and reports: not shipped, and they carry fixtures ───────
# ⚠️ `apps/e2e` HOLDS LIVE-SUITE CREDENTIALS AT RUNTIME and Playwright traces
# after a failure. Neither belongs in an image that gets pushed to a registry.
apps/e2e
apps/storybook
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/coverage
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts

# ── documentation and working notes ─────────────────────────────────────────
docs
reviews
ai-coworkers
*.md
!README.md
